I have a new idea. What about a scroll of honning, or sharpening. These 
scrolls would give temporary plusses to the weapons. Normal scrolls would give
a temporary +1, blessed scrolls would increase the dammage roll perminantly, 
or untill the weapon is missused, and cursed scrolls would dull the blade 
perminantly, or untill sharpened. On the down side Plusses from shaarpening 
wouldn't be considered magical or increase your to hit ability. But on the 
plus side the bonus side if you have a +8 unsharpened sword you can use 
sharpening to add a plus without risk of destroying the blade. You could 
however sharpen the blade too much and get the message "You have 
sharpened your {weapon in use} down to dagger." or "Your dagger has been 
sharpened down to a hilt." Blunt weapos couldn't be sharpened, and the 
blessed sharpness of blade is much more likely to be lost than normal 
enchantment.
Another item would be a sharpening stone, a normal one would remove minuses 
from and uncursed weapon, a cused one would dull the blade, and a blessed one 
could temporarly increase the damage bonus.

